{"config":{"lang":["en"],"separator":"[\\s\\-]+","pipeline":["stopWordFilter"],"fields":{"title":{"boost":1000.0},"text":{"boost":1.0},"tags":{"boost":1000000.0}}},"docs":[{"location":"","title":"Calculus Interactive Guide","text":"<p>Instructions: Type your answer and press ENTER.</p>"},{"location":"#1-sequence-limits","title":"1. Sequence Limits","text":""},{"location":"#definition","title":"Definition","text":"<p>A sequence \\(a_n\\) approaches a limit \\(L\\) if the terms get infinitely close to \\(L\\) as \\(n \\to \\infty\\).</p>"},{"location":"#example","title":"Example","text":"<p>Find: \\(\\lim_{n \\to \\infty} \\frac{2n + 1}{n}\\)</p> <p>Solution: $\\(\\frac{2n}{n} + \\frac{1}{n} = 2 + \\frac{1}{n} \\implies 2 + 0 = 2\\)$</p>"},{"location":"#practice","title":"Practice","text":"<p>Find limit of \\(a_n = \\frac{n+1}{n}\\).</p> <p>Answer:</p> <p></p> Show Solution <p>Divide by \\(n\\): $\\(\\lim_{n \\to \\infty} (1 + 1/n) = 1\\)$</p>"},{"location":"#2-function-limits","title":"2. Function Limits","text":""},{"location":"#definition_1","title":"Definition","text":"<p>Limits describe the behavior of a function near a point, even if the point itself is undefined (like \\(0/0\\)).</p>"},{"location":"#example_1","title":"Example","text":"<p>Find: \\(\\lim_{x \\to 3} \\frac{x^2 - 9}{x - 3}\\)</p> <p>Solution: Factorize: \\(\\frac{(x-3)(x+3)}{x-3} = x+3\\). Result: \\(3+3=6\\).</p>"},{"location":"#practice_1","title":"Practice","text":"<p>Find limit of \\(f(x) = \\frac{x^2 - 1}{x - 1}\\) as \\(x \\to 1\\).</p> <p>Answer:</p> <p></p> Show Solution <p>Factor: \\((x-1)(x+1)\\). Result: \\(2\\).</p>"},{"location":"#3-indeterminate-forms","title":"3. Indeterminate Forms","text":""},{"location":"#definition_2","title":"Definition","text":"<p>The form \\(0/0\\) requires algebraic manipulation (factoring, conjugate, L'Hopital) to resolve.</p>"},{"location":"#example_2","title":"Example","text":"<p>Find: \\(\\lim_{x \\to 0} \\frac{5x^2 + 10x}{x}\\)</p> <p>Solution: Factor \\(x\\): \\(\\frac{x(5x+10)}{x} = 5x+10\\). Result: \\(10\\).</p>"},{"location":"#practice_2","title":"Practice","text":"<p>Find limit of \\(f(x) = \\frac{2x^2 - 2}{x - 1}\\) as \\(x \\to 1\\).</p> <p>Answer:</p> <p></p> Show Solution <p>Simplify: \\(2(x+1) \\to 4\\).</p>"},{"location":"#final-test","title":"Final Test","text":""},{"location":"#task-a","title":"Task A","text":"<p>Limit of \\(a_n = \\frac{3n}{n+2}\\).</p> <p></p> Solution <p>Highest power coeff: \\(3\\).</p>"},{"location":"#task-b","title":"Task B","text":"<p>Limit of \\(f(x) = \\frac{x^2 + 3x}{x}\\) as \\(x \\to 0\\).</p> <p></p> Solution <p>Simplify: \\(x+3 \\to 3\\).</p>"}]}